{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1214629-immaculate-and-sorcery","id":1214629,"title":"Immaculate and Sorcery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-03T09:00:38-07:00","id":1214629,"title":"Immaculate and Sorcery","content":"So I had a character concept of an immaculate monk who prior to meeting up with the party spent their days traveling around the inner sea and especially river provinces in their floral ferry, delivering medicine, music, guidance and the iron fist of justice against spirits.<br /> <br /> How lore friendly is that? Is there any stigma around sorcery in the order that anyone can remember?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T09:08:14-07:00","id":1214633,"title":"","content":"According to Immaculate lore, then sorcery was discovered/invented by one of the Imaculate dragons to defeat the anathema<br /> <br /> ...so, there's nothing against it that way around. Demons, spirits, elementals - according to immaculate doctrine they are all subservient to the spiritually enlightened DBs.<br /> <br /> of course, studying at Heptagram might be a bit of a dogmatic challenge for a monk due to the anathema-made books and scrolls in their libraries.<br /> <br /> <br /> but if you can get a sorcery teacher from somewhere else, then it should make sense. A lot of sorcery could support a monk in dealing with rogue spirits and gods, or for fighting anathema","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T09:16:52-07:00","id":1214635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1214629-immaculate-and-sorcery?p=1214633#post1214633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but if you can get a sorcery teacher from somewhere else, then it should make sense. A lot of sorcery could support a monk in dealing with rogue spirits and gods, or for fighting anathema</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh I like this idea. It opens up a lot of cool options for a unique mentor, like an old monk who\u2019s also gone down this path, or maybe some god or elemental that I\u2019ve encountered in my travels and formed a bond with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T09:18:29-07:00","id":1214636,"title":"","content":"I would point out that mnemon learned sorcery in this edition while being sheltered from Ragara by the immaculate order.<br /> <br /> One of my players is initiating into sorcery through discovering ancient meditative texts (precursors to the immaculate styles) which help him realize how to manipulate the flow of essence within creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T09:23:45-07:00","id":1214641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1214629-immaculate-and-sorcery#post1214629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How lore friendly is that? Is there any stigma around sorcery in the order that anyone can remember?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's a specific one beyond the general attitude of the Realm, but it does strike me that aspects of the monastic lifestyle might generaaly be a bit incompatible with sorcery.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, you already seem to have ideas about this character that would make them a bit unorthodox. I could see a character that is still a member of the Order. but quietly discouraged from ever taking up residence in the temples again.<br /> <br /> \u200bEither that or somebody who joined the Order later in life, after already initiating. We have, after all, a sample monk who did not become so until living to the old age of a Dragon Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T09:44:36-07:00","id":1214648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1214629-immaculate-and-sorcery?p=1214641#post1214641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think there's a specific one beyond the general attitude of the Realm, but it does strike me that aspects of the monastic lifestyle might generaaly be a bit incompatible with sorcery.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, you already seem to have ideas about this character that would make them a bit unorthodox. I could see a character that is still a member of the Order. but quietly discouraged from ever taking up residence in the temples again.<br /> <br /> \u200bEither that or somebody who joined the Order later in life, after already initiating. We have, after all, a sample monk who did not become so until living to the old age of a Dragon Blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right that\u2019s true. I was originally thinking that he might have joined to escape some marriage deal and sort of found his calling there. Ironically helping people to understand that their role in the perfected hierarchy is often an unpleasant and thankless one, and trying to escape that role can be ruinous to all. <br /> <br /> That could lead to the order being all \u201clook he\u2019s an exalt so of course we\u2019re happy to have him, but maybe he can wander off to go be a missionary off where he\u2019s not seen much at home. Like that parrot monk we\u2019ve got.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T10:19:07-07:00","id":1214664,"title":"","content":"What aspects of Sorcery are incompatible with a monsatic lifestyle?<br /> <br /> I think 3e Sorcery has such a broad thematic range that such classifications are generally short handing this system statement.<br /> <br /> We have a shaping ritual which is basically enlightenment through asceticism, even having merits related to your body, deprivation, abdication and the elements. How is that incompatible with a monastic lifestyle?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T11:41:19-07:00","id":1214698,"title":"","content":"I didn't say &quot;a lifestyle&quot; I said &quot;<u>the</u> lifestyle&quot;. Of Immaculate monks specifically. I assume that, by and large, the mannerisms of Immaculate monks are incompatible with the regular use of sorcery, either in terms of the shaping rituals or the spells or workings. From my understanding and assumptions, the kind of asceticism in that particular initiation would be offensive to Immaculates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T11:56:20-07:00","id":1214706,"title":"","content":"Hmm... Yah... I won't pretend to understand Immaculate lifestyle enough to make a judgement on that.<br /> <br /> Can you be a bit more specific in what way you see that specific shaping ritual and the Immaculate monastic lifestyle clashing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T15:37:55-07:00","id":1214796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1214629-immaculate-and-sorcery?p=1214635#post1214635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooh I like this idea. It opens up a lot of cool options for a unique mentor, like an old monk who\u2019s also gone down this path, or maybe some god or elemental that I\u2019ve encountered in my travels and formed a bond with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One side: Sidereal","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T15:50:29-07:00","id":1214806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1214629-immaculate-and-sorcery?p=1214698#post1214698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say &amp;quot;a lifestyle&amp;quot; I said &amp;quot;<u>the</u> lifestyle&amp;quot;. Of Immaculate monks specifically. I assume that, by and large, the mannerisms of Immaculate monks are incompatible with the regular use of sorcery, either in terms of the shaping rituals or the spells or workings. From my understanding and assumptions, the kind of asceticism in that particular initiation would be offensive to Immaculates.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like you are defining the possible initiations into sorcery as far too narrow. That particular initiation may not be kosher, but it does not mean the player and the ST can not together craft an initiation that doesn\u2019t negatively interact with immaculate mores and thematics. The core book says \u201cA few sorcerers forge their own path\u2014following contemplative or meditative disciplines that purify and enlighten the mind...\u201d this style of self discipline can totally work within the structures of the immaculate order in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}